/-!
# Results cited in Graph Minors IX

*Graph Minors. IX. Disjoint crossed paths* (JCTB 49 (1990) 40–77) uses Menger's theorem
(`GraphMinor.menger`) and the Erdős–Szekeres theorem (its reference [1]), which must be
proved. In the proof of (10.1) (page 65) it follows the proof of Graph Minors III, (4.1), which is
formalized directly as a lemma in `GraphMinor/GM09/`. The references [3-6] are not used: the paper
names them only as earlier proofs of a characterization that it proves again.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace GraphMinor.GM09

end GraphMinor.GM09
